# Supabase and PostgreSQL

- Read `DATABASE.md` and `ENVIRONMENTS.md`; verify current Supabase docs/changelog and installed CLI behavior before implementation.
- Prefer permanent documents named in `README.md` over `RIDEVECTOR_HANDOFF.md`.
- Use declarative schemas as source of truth with generated migrations reviewed before apply; never rewrite an applied migration.
- Use separate local/development/staging/production resources per `ENVIRONMENTS.md`. Milestone 0 (ADR-016) requires verified local Supabase plus one live remote `ridevector-development` in `us-west-1`; do not create live `ridevector-staging` or `ridevector-production` yet. Create live remotes only in order local → development during Milestone 0.
- Development must not default to production IDs, hosts, or credentials, and must not resolve deferred staging/production Supabase credentials. Production must always be explicit.
- Enable RLS on every exposed table and test anonymous, owner, other-user, reassignment, and privileged paths.
- `TO authenticated` is not ownership authorization. Use indexed ownership predicates; UPDATE needs SELECT plus `USING` and `WITH CHECK`.
- Never authorize from user-editable metadata. Treat JWT/app-metadata freshness deliberately.
- Keep service-role/secret keys and database credentials out of React/iOS code, bundles, logs, fixtures, and committed files.
- Store secrets in platform-native Supabase mechanisms only for database credentials/secrets in Milestone 0.
- Treat views and `SECURITY DEFINER` functions as security-sensitive; prefer security-invoker behavior and unexposed schemas.
- Use constraints and suitable types for invariants, index foreign keys/RLS predicates based on access paths, and measure before speculative optimization.
- Run migration verification, RLS tests, and database/security advisors available in the selected toolchain; report exactly what ran.
- Milestone 0 establishes workflow and conventions without product tables. Geometry storage format/ownership is decided before the first route-geometry migration, not in Milestone 0 product schema work.
